<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Comancheria</h1><p class="st-meta">1706 CE – 1875 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The domain of the Comanche, a horse-borne power of the southern Plains that dominated trade and raiding from Kansas to deep into Mexico.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a>, or Numunuu, split from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshone">Shoshone</a> in the Great Basin and moved onto the southern Plains in the early 18th century, first appearing in Spanish records at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taos-new-mexico">Taos</a> in 1706. Mastering the horse, they drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apache">Apache</a> south and by mid-century controlled a territory stretching across western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kansas">Kansas</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> society was organised in independent divisions, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penateka">Penateka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamparika">Yamparika</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kotsoteka">Kotsoteka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nokoni">Nokoni</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwahadi">Kwahadi</a>, each with its own chiefs, who met in councils. Vast horse herds and bison hunting underpinned an economy of trade and raiding, with captives, horses and robes exchanged at New Mexican fairs. In 1786 the chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecueracapa">Ecueracapa</a> made peace with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/santa-fe-de-nuevo-mexico">Santa Fe de Nuevo Mexico</a>, and raids into northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mexico">Mexico</a> later reached as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durango-city">Durango</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Epidemics, wars with Texans and the slaughter of the bison weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-war">Red River War</a> of 1874 to 1875 the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwahadi">Kwahadi</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanah-parker">Quanah Parker</a>, surrendered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-sill">Fort Sill</a>, and the Comanche were settled on a reservation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/comancheria.jpg" alt="Comancheria" width="320" height="545"><figcaption>Image: User:Plumber and Bill Nelson · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Comancheria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1706 CE – 1875 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ecueracapa, Buffalo Hump, Quanah Parker</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Comanche traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Comanche</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a>, <a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Comanche Nation, Numunuu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1790&amp;focus=comancheria" aria-label="Comancheria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2283 755 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Comancheria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2570 1008h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2603 1011h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2603 1011h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United States. 